# Entry Main: a lone @ outside the record `return: @` is the prefix operator without its operand, and construction
# still refuses it (the book #operand-storage; the builder, lm_graph_build_expression). The right side of the write is
# the atom @ alone: the builder answers 2, before any launch; nothing is executed.
int: r 0
---
Main:
    node\r := @
